From e28f703a2bf05b7e1868940603a3d6988f3f714f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruzzil <1434309+cruzzil@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:00:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix PLIO compressed tile buffer overflow

imcomp_calc_max_elem() sized the PLIO output buffer at nx * sizeof(int),
i.e. 2 shorts per pixel, but pl_p2li() writes a 7 short line list header
followed by up to 3 shorts per pixel: 2 to encode a pixel value that
differs from the previous one by more than 4095, plus 1 for the run
length.  imcomp_compress_tile() therefore handed pl_p2li() a buffer that
could be far too small, and pl_p2li() had no way to know how big it was.

Compressing a 3x3 image with PLIO overran a 12 byte heap block; with
worst case data the overflow happens at every image size, running about
50% past the end of the buffer.  Reported as heasarc/cfitsio#136.

Size the buffer at (3 * nx + 7) shorts, which is the largest line list
pl_p2li() can produce, and pass the buffer length to pl_p2li() so that it
returns an error instead of writing past the end if the estimate is ever
wrong again.  This mirrors pl_l2pi(), which already takes a srclen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fitsio2.h               |  2 +-
 imcompress.c            | 11 ++++-
 pliocomp.c              | 23 ++++++++--
 tests/test_imcompress.c | 87 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test_pliocomp.c   | 96 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 5 files changed, 207 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/imcompress.c b/imcompress.c
index fe571596..d0c8c485 100644
--- a/imcompress.c
+++ b/imcompress.c
@@ -1476,6 +1476,15 @@ int imcomp_calc_max_elem (int comptype, int nx, int zbitpix, int blocksize)
         else
             return( (int) (nx * 4.4 + 26));   /* will be compressing 32-bit int array */
     }
+    else if (comptype == PLIO_1)
+    {
+        /* pl_p2li writes a 7 short header, followed by at most 3 shorts per
+	   pixel (2 to encode a pixel value that differs from the previous one
+	   by more than 4095, plus 1 for the run length).  Note that this is
+	   larger than the uncompressed 32-bit array for small tiles. */
+
+        return((int) ((3 * (size_t) nx + 7) * sizeof(short)));
+    }
     else
         return(nx * sizeof(int));
 }
